index=soc_agent_demo sourcetype="soc:agent:vulnerability"
    run_id="<RUN_ID_FROM_GENERATOR_OUTPUT>"
    earliest=0 latest=now
| eval cvss=tonumber(cvss)
| eval priority_rule=case(
    known_exploited="yes"
        AND (internet_facing="yes" OR asset_criticality="critical"), "R1",
    known_exploited="yes"
        OR (cvss>=9 AND internet_facing="yes"), "R2",
    cvss>=7, "R3",
    true(), "R4"
  )
| eval priority=case(
    priority_rule="R1", "P1",
    priority_rule="R2", "P2",
    priority_rule="R3", "P3",
    priority_rule="R4", "P4"
  )
| eval priority_reason=case(
    priority_rule="R1",
      "Known-exploited flag yes AND (internet-facing yes OR asset criticality critical)",
    priority_rule="R2",
      "R1 not matched; known-exploited flag yes OR (CVSS >= 9 AND internet-facing yes)",
    priority_rule="R3",
      "R1 and R2 not matched; CVSS >= 7",
    priority_rule="R4",
      "No higher-priority demo rule matched"
  )
| eval finding_evidence="finding_id=".finding_id
    ."; asset=".asset
    ."; cvss=".cvss
    ."; internet_facing=".internet_facing
    ."; asset_criticality=".asset_criticality
    ."; known_exploited=".known_exploited
    ."; exploitation_on_asset=".exploitation_on_asset
    ."; synthetic=".synthetic
    ."; priority_policy=".priority_policy
    ."; priority_rule=".priority_rule
    ."; priority=".priority
    ."; priority_reason=".priority_reason
| stats
    count as finding_count
    count(eval(priority="P1")) as p1_count
    count(eval(priority="P2")) as p2_count
    count(eval(priority="P3")) as p3_count
    count(eval(priority="P4")) as p4_count
    values(finding_evidence) as finding_records
    by run_id
| eval evidence=mvjoin(finding_records," || ")
| fields run_id finding_count p1_count p2_count p3_count p4_count evidence
| aiagent agent_name="VulnPriorityAdvisor" prompt="Produce a concise vulnerability prioritisation briefing from the supplied synthetic evidence.

RUN:
run_id={run_id}
finding_count={finding_count}
P1={p1_count}
P2={p2_count}
P3={p3_count}
P4={p4_count}

PRIORITY PROVENANCE:
Upstream SPL calculated priorities using the demo_v1 lab policy.
Rules were evaluated in order, and the first matching rule determined priority:
R1 assigns P1 when known_exploited=yes AND (internet_facing=yes OR asset_criticality=critical).
R2 assigns P2 to remaining findings when known_exploited=yes OR (cvss>=9 AND internet_facing=yes).
R3 assigns P3 to remaining findings when cvss>=7.
R4 assigns P4 to all remaining findings.
These are synthetic demonstration rules, not an approved production remediation policy.

FINDING EVIDENCE:
{evidence}

INSTRUCTIONS:
Preserve all supplied priorities, counts, matched rules, and field values.
State that upstream SPL assigned priorities using demo_v1; do not say the assignment method is missing.
Do not claim that you calculated priorities.
For each finding, explain the actual supported rule branches, not every possible OR branch.
A known-exploited flag does not prove exploitation of the listed asset.
A false known-exploited flag does not prove absence of exploitation.
Preserve exploitation_on_asset=not_assessed.
Do not infer business functions or impact from hostnames.
Do not invent CVEs, patches, owners, deadlines, or completed actions.
Do not search or call tools.

OUTPUT:
Use plain text without Markdown symbols, tables, or pipe-delimited output.
Keep the briefing under 400 words.
Return:
Executive summary with total findings, priority distribution, and SPL priority provenance.
Four numbered findings, each stating finding ID, asset, priority, matched rule, and supported reason.
Recommended analyst validation steps.
Missing information and limitations.
Explicitly identify the evidence as synthetic demonstration data."
| table agent_name status result_1 error
